{"event": "artifact", "agent": "documentation", "file": "README.md", "content": "# Password Validator\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe `PasswordValidator` application provides a function to validate passwords based on specific criteria. It checks if the password meets the following requirements:\n- Is a string\n- At least 8 characters long\n- Contains an uppercase letter\n- Contains a lowercase letter\n- Contains a digit\n- Contains at least one special character from `!@#$%^&*`\n\n## API\n\n### Function: `validate_password(password)`\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `password` (str): The password to be validated.\n\n**Returns:**\n- A dictionary containing two keys:\n  - `valid` (bool): Indicates whether the password is valid or not.\n  - `errors` (list[str]): A list of error messages indicating which validation rules were not met.\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom app import validate_password\n\nresult = validate_password(\"Example123!\")\nprint(result)\n```\n\nOutput:\n```json\n{\n    \"valid\": True,\n    \"errors\": []\n}\n```\n\n## Running Pytest\n\nTo run the tests using `pytest`, follow these steps:\n\n1. Ensure you have `pytest` installed. If not, install it using pip:\n   ```sh\n   pip install pytest\n   ```\n\n2. Run the tests by executing the following command in your terminal:\n   ```sh\n   pytest\n   ```\n\nThis will execute all the test cases defined in your project and provide a report on the test results."}
